# Dart / Flutter Style

- Use `final` by default; use `const` for compile-time constants and const widgets.
- Add `const` to widget constructors wherever possible for rebuild performance.
- Prefer named parameters with `required` for widget constructors.
- Extract large `build()` trees into smaller widgets, not private helper methods returning `Widget`.

## Async & null safety

```dart
// ❌ BAD: force-unwrap and unhandled future
final user = users.firstWhere((u) => u.id == id)!;
fetchProfile();

// ✅ GOOD: handle absence and await
final user = users.where((u) => u.id == id).firstOrNull;
if (user == null) return;
await fetchProfile();
```

- Avoid `!` (bang) operator; handle null explicitly.
- Always `await` futures or intentionally use `unawaited(...)`.
- Dispose controllers/streams in `dispose()`.

